  "id": "typicality-effect",
  "term": "typicality effect",
  "definition": "The typicality effect is a pattern in which memory or recognition differs depending on how well an object fits its usual context. In the supplied study, objects that were typical for a setting were recognized less well than context-atypical objects, showing that contextual fit can shape how objects are perceived and remembered.",
